@startuml vehicle_step_sequence
title vehicle::step: one 1 kHz step of the whole tractor
autonumber
participant "Caller\n(pull::step, tool, test)" as Caller
participant "vehicle::step" as Step
participant "driveline" as Driveline
participant "chassis" as Chassis
participant "engine" as Engine
participant "tire" as Tire
participant "solve_chain" as Solve
participant "clutch::resolve" as Clutch

Caller -> Step : step(state, model, {throttle, clutch_pedal, gear, steering, brakes},\n  Ground{rear_left, rear_right, front surface}, Drawbar{pull, lift, side}, dt_s)
opt requested gear differs
  Step -> Driveline : shift(gear, clutch capacity == 0)
end
Step -> Chassis : axle_loads(state, drawbar)
Chassis --> Step : rear / front / wheelie bar load
loop left and right side (wheel speed = axle ∓ differential,\n  ground speed = u ∓ yaw rate · track / 2)
  Step -> Tire : traction(wheel speed, ground speed, load per tire, that side's surface)
  Tire --> Step : force, slope (linearized), slip
end
Step -> Tire : driven_rolling_resistance(rear load per tire, slip, each side's surface)
Step -> Tire : thrown_soil_m3_s(rear load per tire, slip, wheel speed, each side's surface)
Step -> Tire : towed_rolling_resistance(front load per tire, front surface)
Step -> Tire : side_grip(front, each rear side); with_traction(that side's grip, traction, full bite, slip)
Step -> Tire : side_force_n(grip, patch deflection) for front and rear
Step -> Engine : predict(throttle)
Step -> Chassis : predict(drawbar pull + front tire and bar rolling drag\n  + steered front tires' side force along the body)
group solve_rear_with_brakes (once; while a brake holds, up to 8 more:\n  Newton steps, then Illinois once one held side is bracketed)
Step -> Driveline : predict(rear rolling resistance + both brakes' torque)
Step -> Step : differential as a line in the common slip change;\n  both sides' traction folded into one TireLine
Step -> Solve : engine line, driveline Response, TireLine, body line
Solve -> Solve : lock torque with the tire force eliminated\n(branch by the torque's sign: gearbox efficiency)
Solve -> Clutch : resolve(capacity, lock torque)
Clutch --> Solve : torque: locked, or kinetic capacity if slipping
Solve -> Solve : tire force for that clutch torque
Solve --> Step : clutch torque, tire force
Step -> Step : end speeds of both sides' wheels;\n  a brake that would carry its side through rest:\n  find the torque that holds it at rest
end
Step -> Engine : advance(load = clutch torque)
Step -> Driveline : advance(clutch torque, axle torque = -r * tire force)
Step -> Step : differential advances
Step -> Chassis : advance_lateral(front, rear and hitch side forces,\n  yaw moment of the sides' unequal traction)
Step -> Chassis : advance(drive force = tire force): moves along the heading
Step -> Tire : relax_deflection_m(front, rear) at the new speeds
Step -> Step : axle torque from the axle's balance
Step -> Chassis : advance_pitch(axle torque, drawbar pull and lift,\n  front rolling resistance)\n(see the pitch step)
Step --> Caller : Output
@enduml
